Module dorothea "The Dorothea" {
  Description "The Dorothea's people: a master in debt, a mate who sells what is not his, a cook who sees everything, a boy, a passenger with a measuring-rod; and a night visitor with a cutter.".

  Person rune "Tobias Rune" at deck {
    Role "mate of the Dorothea". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "sailor".
    Greets "A long man in a patched jersey who looks as if he has been folded up and put away wet. 'Mate,' he says, touching his cap. 'Tobias Rune. Don't mind the Captain, she speaks to the sea and the sea has never answered back. She likes that in a friend.'".
  }
  Person mab "Mab Hallam" at forecastle {
    Role "cook". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Mab Hallam stirs a pot the size of a font with a spoon the size of a boat-hook, and has not looked up since you came down the ladder. 'I've fed forty crews on this ship,' she says. 'I've fed three that were hanged and two that were bishops and I couldn't tell you which was which by the manners.'".
  }
  Person nipper "Nipper" at deck {
    Role "ship's boy". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "A boy of about eleven, barefoot on the cold deck, looks you up and down with the frank hostility of someone who has been told a landsman is coming and what will be expected of him.".
  }
  Person quint "Odile Quint" at deck {
    Role "a surveyor of the Collegium of Measures, bound for the Pharos". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "scholar".
    Joins "Odile Quint closes her pocket-book on a finger, takes her ell-rod under her arm, and falls in at your elbow, a little too close, as someone who measures people measures them.".
    Leaves "Odile Quint nods once. 'I shall be at the Collegium of Measures at Sennet,' she says. 'Ask for the junior Fellow who is always right.'".
    Carries old_glossary.
    Greets "A narrow woman in a grey coat is seated on a cask with a brass ell-rod across her knees, looking not at the sea but at a pocket-book of figures. She does not look up. 'Odile Quint,' she says. 'Collegium of Measures, Sennet. If you're sick, be sick to leeward. If you're not, I'd like a word about your idea of a straight line.'".
  }
  Initially Assert acceptsEscort(quint, party).

  Topic rune_cargo with rune "Ask Rune how the Dorothea does for money" when true once {
    Says "'Sixty crowns of the Orsett factor's money in her keel, and every penny's got a face on it that looks at the Captain,' says Rune. He laughs without sound. 'You'd think a woman could sell enough salt.' He looks, for just a moment, at the after hatch.".
  }
  Topic mab_rune with mab "Ask Mab what she thinks of the mate" when true once {
    Says "'Rune's the best hand I ever sailed with,' says Mab, 'and I wouldn't leave a spoon where he could see it. He loves her, you know. The Captain. Not that way. The way a dog loves a person that's never once been nice to it.' She tastes the pot. 'He sold two casks of the Pharos oil in Orsett in the spring. She's not counted them yet. When she does I'd sooner be on deck.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rune_sells). }
  }
  Discovery rune_sells "The mate, Tobias Rune, has been selling the Pharos's lamp-oil out of the Dorothea's hold, two casks at a time, to make up the Captain's debt before she finds out how deep it is.".
  Topic quint_rod with quint "Ask Odile Quint what the Collegium wants with the Pharos" when true once {
    Says "'It is a unit,' she says. 'A very good one. Seven feet and some inches of a measure that is not a foot and not a yard, and has its own sixths, and has been the length of the Pharos stair and the width of its door and the height of its lamp for as long as anybody has measured. The Aeneans wrote it on a bronze table in the tower, and thought it was theirs.' She taps the ell-rod. 'I would like to lay mine against it. I would like to know whether we have been using the right one.'".
  }
  Topic quint_pharos with quint "Ask Odile Quint who the Pharos's builders were" when true once {
    Says "She smiles a very small smile. 'You'll hear that Aeneans built it. The Aeneans cut a line over the door and said it was theirs. Have you looked at the joints? I have looked at the joints through a lens. They are better than the Aeneans' best. Whoever made the tower had a measure that was not in use when the Aeneans came, and the Aeneans, to their credit, wrote it down.'".
  }

  // ── The night visitor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Jago Pendry's cutter, the Kestrel, does a night's business on this passage as other masters take the air. What the
  // company sees, what it does about it, and who is told, decide what the mate is to the Captain at the Combs.
  Person jago "Jago Pendry" at nowhere {
    Role "master of the cutter Kestrel". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 4. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "sailor".
    Greets "Jago Pendry sits on the Dorothea's rail as if the ship were his and he were merely letting her sail. 'Good evening,' he says. 'Don't get up. I'm only passing the time with Mr Rune.'".
  }
  Relation hailed(entity). Relation sold(entity). Relation told(group). Relation bribed(group). Relation shamed(group). Relation looked(group).
  Rule kestrel_hails when at(hull, open_sea) and progress(hull) >= 66 and not hailed(hull) and not troubled(hull)
    says "A light has been following the Dorothea since dusk, low, to leeward. Now it closes. A cutter slides under the lee quarter without a word spoken, a long dark vessel with a mast like a thought, and a man in a good coat steps over the rail and onto your deck as if it were a drawing room. Rune is at the after hatch before anyone has seen him go." {
    Assert hailed(hull). Assert at(jago, deck). Set hailAt(hull) to watch(clock).
  }
  Measure hailAt(entity).
  // Left alone, Pendry takes what Rune sells and goes: the casks are the Captain's loss by morning.
  Rule jago_leaves when at(jago, deck) and watch(clock) >= hailAt(hull) + 24 and not sold(hull)
    says "Jago Pendry finishes his business with the mate, nods to the company as to old acquaintances, and goes back over the rail with two casks on a line. The cutter slides off to leeward. It is not mentioned again." {
    Retract at(jago, deck). Assert sold(hull). Decrease cargo(hull) by 4. Assert quiet(hull).
  }
  Relation quiet(entity).
  Observe jago_deck at deck when at(jago, deck) and not sold(hull) "Jago Pendry and Tobias Rune stand together at the after hatch, talking low. Two casks are on the hatch-cover between them, and neither is looking at the casks.".
  Action watch_the_hatch(actor: group, site: place) "Watch what passes at the after hatch" {
    Description "Not hiding. Only being where somebody can be seen to be.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and at(jago, deck) and not looked(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert looked(actor). Assert knows(actor, rune_sells). }
    Result "You watch the two men for as long as it takes to make a cask change hands. Jago hands Rune a purse. Rune hands Jago the cask. Neither of them thinks it is anything but a tender thing between friends. Nipper, on the rail with his back to them, is crying without noise.".
    Otherwise "You watch, and see nothing but two men talking, and one of them is looking back at you.".
  }
  Topic jago_cut with jago "Ask Jago Pendry what he buys" when looked(actor) or knows(actor, rune_sells) once {
    Says "'Whatever a good man sells,' says Jago. 'The Pharos oil is the best on the coast. Clean, no smoke. I pay Rune what Orsett pays and he gets to feel like a rogue and not a thief.' He studies you. 'I'll make you a proposal. You saw nothing, and I saw nothing, and here is eight coin to make the nothing mutual.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(jago). }
  }
  Relation offered(entity).
  Topic take_cut with jago "Take Jago Pendry's eight coin" when offered(jago) and not bribed(actor) and not shamed(actor) and not told(actor) once {
    Says "He puts the coin in your hand, and for a moment you are in the same trade. 'Sensible,' he says, and goes back over the rail as lightly as he came, with two casks on a line behind him, and the cutter slides back into the dark. Nobody on the Dorothea says a word of it, then or after. In the morning the hold is a little lighter and the Captain does not look at the tally.".
    On discuss { Assert bribed(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 8. Assert sold(hull). Retract at(jago, deck). Decrease cargo(hull) by 4. }
  }
  Topic tell_bascom with bascom "Tell Captain Bascom what you saw at the after hatch" when (looked(actor) or knows(actor, rune_sells)) and not told(actor) and not shamed(actor) and not bribed(actor) once {
    Says "She hears you out without a word. Then she takes the pipe out and walks aft along the deck with the unhurried step of a woman who has decided to do the thing she has been putting off. 'Mr Pendry,' she says. 'Mr Rune.' Her voice does not change. Jago is over the rail before she reaches the hatch, with a flourish and no casks. Rune stands where he is. 'Eleven casks,' she says. 'In the spring I made it fourteen. I told myself I'd counted wrong.' She looks at him a long time. 'You will stand your watch. You will not touch the wheel. When we raise Skerrow you will go ashore with your bag.' Rune opens his mouth. 'Don't,' says Bascom, gently, and that is the worst of it.".
    On discuss { Assert told(actor). Retract at(jago, deck). Assert disgraced(rune). }
  }
  Relation disgraced(group).
  Topic shame_rune with rune "Take Rune aside and say what you saw" when (looked(actor) or knows(actor, rune_sells)) and not told(actor) and not shamed(actor) and not bribed(actor) once {
    Says "'It isn't what it looks like,' says Rune, and his mouth goes on trying, and then he stops. He looks at Nipper's back. 'It's exactly what it looks like.' He sits down on the hatch-cover. 'She's been good to me,' he says. 'She's been better to me than anyone and I've been robbing her for a year to keep her in the Orsett man's good books, and every cask I sold made it worse.' He puts both hands over his face. 'Tell me what to do.'".
    On discuss { Assert shamed(actor). Assert indebted(rune, actor). }
  }
  Relation indebted(group, group).
  Action unload_casks(actor: group, site: place) "Make Rune and Jago Pendry put the casks back" {
    Description "Pendry is a smuggler and a gentleman. He has no wish to fight on another man's deck.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and at(jago, deck) and shamed(actor) and not sold(hull).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert sold(hull). Retract at(jago, deck). }
    On failure { Retract at(kestrel_hands, nowhere). Assert at(kestrel_hands, deck). }
    Result "Rune lifts the first cask back onto his shoulder and carries it to the hatch, and Jago Pendry watches him do it, and watches the company's faces, and does a sum. 'Another time,' he says, with real regret, and steps over the rail. The cutter's light goes out as it left, one thing at a time.".
    Otherwise "Pendry only smiles, and holds out his hand for the purse he has already paid, and Rune cannot give it back because he has already spent it.".
  }

  // If the company pushes and cannot push hard enough, Pendry does not argue. He whistles, and his hands come over the rail
  // with belaying-pins. They can be fought; they can be paid; the Captain can be fetched; or the mate, if he is the
  // company's, can say a word, and they are Rune's old friends.
  Person kestrel_hands "the Kestrel's hands" at nowhere {
    Role "three hard men off the cutter with belaying-pins". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 2. Numbers 3. Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Three men are over the rail and on the deck of the Dorothea before anyone saw the cutter's boat. The nearest hefts a belaying-pin, not as a threat but as a sort of punctuation.".
    Comes "The nearest says, 'Don't make it into a thing,' and the belaying-pin comes round in a flat, practised arc.".
  }
  Relation handsPaid(group). Relation handsSent(group).
  Action pay_the_hands(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Kestrel's hands eight coin to go back over the rail" {
    Description "It is cheaper than a head. It is also eight coin that will be spent on drink by the next watch.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and at(kestrel_hands, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 8 and not handsPaid(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 8. Assert handsPaid(actor). Retract at(kestrel_hands, deck). Assert at(kestrel_hands, nowhere). Retract at(jago, deck). Assert sold(hull). Decrease cargo(hull) by 4. }
    Result "The tallest looks at the coin, and at the company, and does a sum his face is not used to doing. 'Eight,' he says. 'For the trouble.' He pockets it with the dignity of a man being paid a fee. They go back over the rail one at a time, and the cutter takes her boat in, and four casks are not in the hold in the morning.".
  }
  Action rune_speaks(actor: group, site: place) "Have Rune speak to the Kestrel's hands, who drank with him in Orsett" {
    Description "He has sold them four casks and a good deal of rum. They like him.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and at(kestrel_hands, site) and indebted(rune, actor) and not handsSent(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert handsSent(actor). Retract at(kestrel_hands, deck). Assert at(kestrel_hands, nowhere). Retract at(jago, deck). Assert sold(hull). }
    Result "'Davy,' says Rune. 'Pike. Hobb.' He is not loud. 'She has a keel and a debt and one cask less than I have wronged her for. Go home.' There is a short and terrible silence in which three hard men look at a mate they have known for ten years, and at the company he has chosen, and then at each other. 'Aye,' says the one called Davy, with something not quite like shame, and they go.".
  }
}
